-<section id="case-study" class="section alt"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">V21 · FIRST COMPLETED COMPANY STAR</p><h2>A proof-bound agent assurance system, built against a public mission-AI design lens.</h2></div><p>The company-specific application path is not a claim of company access. It is a bounded way to convert public role requirements into inspected code, an implemented remedy, reproduced proof, and defensible application language.</p></div><div class="star-case"><article class="card star-story"><p class="eyebrow">FROM REQUIREMENT TO PROOF</p><h3>Mission Agentic AI Assurance</h3><p>The reference implementation was iterated past happy-path success. Review exposed concurrency, non-finite metric, canonicalization, evidence-binding, and post-side-effect failure problems; those defects were repaired before proof promotion.</p><div class="star-chain"><div><b>Public role evidence</b><span>1 bounded role record</span></div><div><b>Public problem evidence</b><span>1 externally supportable system problem</span></div><div><b>Inspected implementation paths</b><span>4 exact repository paths</span></div><div><b>Bounded remedy</b><span>1 architecture contract</span></div><div><b>Implementation receipt</b><span>1 implemented reference</span></div><div><b>Reproduced proof</b><span>1 exact deterministic receipt</span></div><div><b>Claim receipt</b><span>1 proof-bound public claim</span></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="button primary small" href="/companies/lockheed-martin/">Open the company dossier</a><a class="button ghost small" href="https://github.com/GlacierEQ/job-application/tree/4328fa7078e6e4125f895768142c6af0c5ec1234/projects/mission-agentic-ai-assurance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Inspect implementation</a></div></article><article class="card star-proof"><p class="eyebrow">MAXIMUM DEFENSIBLE CLAIM</p><h3>What the proof actually earns.</h3><div class="claim-box"><strong>PROOF_BOUND</strong><p>Built and reproducibly tested an independent mission-agent assurance gateway combining content-bound public provenance snapshots, deterministic receipts, thread-safe single-process idempotency, finite-metric drift gating, policy decisions, and circuit breaking, using public mission-AI requirements as a bounded design lens.</p></div><div class="limit-box"><strong>Explicit ceiling:</strong> no Lockheed Martin deployment, adoption, affiliation, employment, endorsement, contract, clearance, proprietary access, distributed exactly-once semantics, production-scale distributed assurance, aerospace/defense certification, or classified-system validation is claimed.</div><div class="receipt-grid"><div class="receipt"><b>17</b><span>acceptance tests</span></div><div class="receipt"><b>3.11–3.13</b><span>Python CI matrix</span></div><div class="receipt"><b>REPRODUCED</b><span>proof state</span></div><div class="receipt"><b>CLAIM_PROMOTED</b><span>Helix stage</span></div></div></article></div></div></section>
