-<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">ROLE FIT</p><h2>Best where model capability meets messy operating reality.</h2></div><p>I am strongest on teams that need a builder to discover the real workflow, define the system boundary, implement the mechanism, and leave behind evidence rather than theater.</p></div><div class="role-proof-grid"><article class="card role-proof"><p class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURE</p><h3>Applied AI Systems Architect</h3><p>Design the contracts and operating boundaries that make AI capability dependable.</p><ul><li>system interfaces, state, and authority</li><li>evaluation and evidence models</li><li>multi-repository architecture</li><li>completion and release design</li></ul></article><article class="card role-proof"><p class="eyebrow">INFRASTRUCTURE</p><h3>Agent Infrastructure Engineer</h3><p>Make agent behavior deterministic enough to reason about, inspect, and recover.</p><ul><li>task ownership and coordination</li><li>tool and connector contracts</li><li>budgets, retries, replay, and refusal</li><li>receipts and durable state</li></ul></article><article class="card role-proof"><p class="eyebrow">DEPLOYMENT</p><h3>Forward-Deployed AI Engineer</h3><p>Translate incomplete real-world requirements into narrow systems that operators can actually use.</p><ul><li>rapid domain discovery</li><li>human-centered implementation</li><li>explicit success criteria</li><li>truthful handoff and repair loops</li></ul></article></div></div></section>
